WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.644
A common misunderstanding is to think of Spark as
PostgreSQL but bigger Spark

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:12.804
is different PostgreSQL is a database system with
transactions constraints indexes

00:00:13.054 --> 00:00:19.355
and stored tables Spark is a distributed compute
engine It

00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:25.972
can query tables and files but its strength is
large-scale analytical processing In

00:00:25.998 --> 00:00:30.932
many real architectures a database and Spark work
together rather than replacing each other
